---
const locations = [
  { id: 'floor', label: 'Basement floor drain', title: 'Basement floor drain backing up', detail: 'A floor drain is usually connected to a trapped branch of the home drainage system. If sewage rises here, the restriction may be farther downstream in a shared building drain or building sewer—not necessarily at the floor drain itself.', clue: 'The washer, toilet, or another fixture may make the floor drain rise or bubble.', next: 'Stop using water if sewage is coming up. A-1 can access and clear the affected drain or sewer line.' },
  { id: 'toilet', label: 'Toilet', title: 'Toilet will not flush or backs up', detail: 'A toilet connects through its own built-in trap to a larger drain branch or soil stack. One toilet acting up can be a local toilet or branch problem. Several fixtures backing up together can point farther downstream.', clue: 'Notice whether a nearby tub, shower, or floor drain gurgles or rises when the toilet is flushed.', next: 'Describe which other fixtures are affected. That pattern helps determine whether the toilet or a shared line needs attention.' },
  { id: 'sink', label: 'Kitchen or bathroom sink', title: 'Sink drains slowly', detail: 'A sink normally drains through a P-trap before joining a branch drain. Grease and food waste are common kitchen restrictions; hair and soap buildup are common at bathroom sinks.', clue: 'If only one sink is slow, its trap or branch may be involved. If several fixtures are affected, the issue may be farther down.', next: 'A-1 can clear an accessible sink branch and help determine whether the restriction is local or shared.' },
  { id: 'shower', label: 'Tub or shower', title: 'Tub or shower drains slowly', detail: 'A tub or shower has a trapped drain that connects to a bathroom branch. Hair and soap buildup can restrict the fixture drain. A backup that appears when another fixture runs may point to a shared branch or main drain.', clue: 'Check whether the toilet or sink in the same bathroom is also slow or gurgling.', next: 'Tell A-1 whether this is the only affected fixture or part of a larger backup.' },
  { id: 'washer', label: 'Washing machine', title: 'Washer standpipe overflows', detail: 'A washing machine pumps discharge water into a standpipe connected to a trapped laundry branch. The washer sends water out quickly, so a partly restricted branch or shared drain may overflow during the pump-out cycle.', clue: 'Water may spill from the standpipe or push up through a nearby floor drain when the washer pumps out.', next: 'Stop running the washer until the drain is checked. Mention whether other fixtures are affected.' },
  { id: 'main', label: 'Several fixtures / main drain', title: 'More than one drain is backing up', detail: 'Fixture branches join larger building drains, which carry wastewater toward the building drain and out to the private building sewer. A restriction in a shared section can affect multiple fixtures, often showing first at a low drain.', clue: 'A toilet affects a tub, the washer makes a floor drain rise, or several fixtures slow down together.', next: 'Stop using water if wastewater is backing up. Call A-1 Drain Cleaning at 641-530-2728.' }
];
---
<section class="bg-white py-12 sm:py-16" aria-labelledby="house-drain-tool-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4">
    <p class="text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[#b4232b]">Explore the plumbing in a typical house</p>
    <h2 id="house-drain-tool-heading" class="mt-2 max-w-4xl text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">Find where the drain problem is showing up.</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-base leading-7 text-slate-700">Choose the fixture or drain that is giving you trouble. The drawing highlights its route through the house toward the sewer. This is a guide to how the system is generally connected—not a diagnosis of your particular piping.</p>

    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[1.2fr_.8fr] lg:items-start">
      <figure class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-[#f1f5f9] p-2 sm:p-4">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 820 560" role="img" aria-labelledby="house-drain-svg-title house-drain-svg-desc" class="block h-auto w-full">
          <title id="house-drain-svg-title">Cutaway of a typical American home's drain, waste, and vent piping</title>
          <desc id="house-drain-svg-desc">A two-level house showing kitchen and bathroom fixtures, toilet, tub, washing machine, basement floor drain, trapped fixture branches, a vent stack through the roof, the building drain, an exterior cleanout, and the private sewer lateral connecting toward the public sewer.</desc>
          <defs>
            <pattern id="house-soil" width="14" height="14" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M0 14L14 0" stroke="#cbd5e1" stroke-width="1"/></pattern>
          </defs>
          <path d="M12 420H808V548H12Z" fill="url(#house-soil)"/>
          <path d="M12 420H808" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="3"/>
          <path d="M80 420V132L330 34L580 132V420Z" fill="#fff" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M58 137L330 24L602 137" fill="none" stroke="#b4232b" stroke-width="10" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M80 275H580M80 420H580" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="5"/>
          <path d="M330 275V420" stroke="#cbd5e1" stroke-width="3"/>
          <text x="330" y="165" fill="#334155" font-size="17" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">UPPER FLOOR</text>
          <text x="330" y="305" fill="#334155" font-size="17" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">MAIN FLOOR</text>
          <text x="330" y="450" fill="#334155" font-size="16" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">BASEMENT</text>

          <!-- Vent stack -->
          <path d="M430 105V92H452V42" fill="none" stroke="#0f766e" stroke-width="10" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M430 92H452" stroke="#0f766e" stroke-width="8"/>
          <text x="470" y="55" fill="#0f766e" font-size="14" font-weight="800">VENT THROUGH ROOF</text>

          <!-- Drain stack and building drain -->
          <path d="M430 105V520H610V540H770" fill="none" stroke="#1d4ed8" stroke-width="13" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M430 105V520H610V540H770" fill="none" stroke="#93c5fd" stroke-width="5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M610 540V420M598 420H622" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="6"/>
          <path d="M770 540V555M750 555H790" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="7" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          <text x="690" y="530" fill="#1e3a8a" font-size="13" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">PRIVATE BUILDING SEWER</text>
          <text x="770" y="550" fill="#334155" font-size="12" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">TOWARD PUBLIC SEWER</text>
          <text x="500" y="505" fill="#1e3a8a" font-size="13" font-weight="800" text-anchor="middle">BUILDING DRAIN</text>
          <text x="635" y="405" fill="#334155" font-size="12" font-weight="700">EXTERIOR CLEANOUT</text>

          <!-- Kitchen sink with P-trap and branch -->
          <path d="M155 205V218Q155 232 169 232H180Q194 232 194 218V210H390V245H430V520" fill="none" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M120 205V185H190V205" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="3"/>
          <path d="M155 205V220Q155 240 175 240" stroke="#1d4ed8" stroke-width="6" fill="none"/>
          <text x="155" y="178" fill="#334155" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">KITCHEN SINK</text>

          <!-- Bathroom lavatory and P-trap -->
          <path d="M265 205V228Q265 242 279 242H290Q304 242 304 228V225H410V260H430V520" fill="none" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M245 205V185H285V205" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="3"/>
          <path d="M265 205V235Q265 255 285 255" stroke="#1d4ed8" stroke-width="6" fill="none"/>
          <text x="265" y="178" fill="#334155" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">BATH SINK</text>

          <!-- Toilet with integral trap and branch -->
          <path d="M130 332V350Q130 370 150 370H270V390H390V520H430" fill="none" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M115 300H160Q178 300 178 318V332H130Q115 332 115 318Z" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="3"/>
          <path d="M130 332V350Q130 370 150 370" stroke="#1d4ed8" stroke-width="7" fill="none"/>
          <text x="145" y="288" fill="#334155" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">TOILET</text>

          <!-- Tub/shower with trap -->
          <path d="M335 326V345Q335 360 350 360H365Q380 360 380 345V400H410V520H430" fill="none" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M280 300H390V326H280Z" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="3"/>
          <path d="M335 326V345Q335 365 355 365" stroke="#1d4ed8" stroke-width="6" fill="none"/>
          <text x="335" y="290" fill="#334155" font-size="13" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">TUB / SHOWER</text>

          <!-- Washer standpipe, trap and branch -->
          <path d="M150 365V400Q150 425 175 425H200V450H390V500H430V520" fill="none" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <rect x="95" y="350" width="45" height="55" rx="4" fill="#e2e8f0" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="3"/>
          <circle cx="117" cy="378" r="13" fill="#fff" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="3"/>
          <path d="M150 365V400Q150 425 175 425" stroke="#1d4ed8" stroke-width="6" fill="none"/>
          <text x="118" y="420" fill="#334155" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">WASHER</text>

          <!-- Floor drain and trap -->
          <path d="M300 415V430Q300 455 325 455H390V500H430V520" fill="none" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <rect x="286" y="410" width="28" height="10" fill="#cbd5e1" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="2"/>
          <path d="M300 415V430Q300 455 325 455" stroke="#1d4ed8" stroke-width="6" fill="none"/>
          <text x="300" y="405" fill="#334155" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">FLOOR DRAIN</text>

          <!-- Route highlights; common downstream route is always visible -->
          <g class="route-highlight" data-route="floor"><path d="M300 415V430Q300 455 325 455H350Q375 455 375 430V470H390V500H430V520H610V540H770" /></g>
          <g class="route-highlight" data-route="toilet"><path d="M130 332V350Q130 370 150 370H270V390H390V520H430V520H610V540H770" /></g>
          <g class="route-highlight" data-route="sink"><path d="M155 205V218Q155 232 169 232H180Q194 232 194 218V210H390V245H430V520H610V540H770M265 205V228Q265 242 279 242H290Q304 242 304 228V225H410V260H430V520H610V540H770" /></g>
          <g class="route-highlight" data-route="shower"><path d="M335 326V345Q335 360 350 360H365Q380 360 380 345V400H410V520H430V520H610V540H770" /></g>
          <g class="route-highlight" data-route="washer"><path d="M150 365V400Q150 425 175 425H200Q225 425 225 400V450H390V500H430V520H610V540H770" /></g>
          <g class="route-highlight" data-route="main"><path d="M430 520H610V540H770" /></g>
          <text x="700" y="390" fill="#334155" font-size="12" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle">OUTSIDE WALL</text>
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="px-2 pb-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600"><span class="font-bold text-blue-800">Blue:</span> drain and waste stack. <span class="font-bold text-teal-700">Green:</span> vent. <span class="font-bold text-amber-700">Orange:</span> selected fixture route. Gray lines show fixture branches. Simplified teaching diagram—not a construction plan. Actual fixture locations, venting, pipe sizes, cleanout locations, and connections vary by house and local code. The private building sewer runs from the building drain toward the public sewer.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5 sm:p-6" aria-labelledby="fixture-choice-heading">
        <h3 id="fixture-choice-heading" class="text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Where are you seeing the problem?</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Choose one to highlight the related drain route.</p>
        <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          {locations.map((item) => <button type="button" class="fixture-choice min-h-12 rounded-md border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3 py-2 text-left text-sm font-bold text-slate-800 hover:border-[#1A1A68] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-[#1A1A68]" data-route={item.id} data-title={item.title} data-detail={item.detail} data-clue={item.clue} data-next={item.next} aria-pressed="false">{item.label}</button>)}
        </div>
        <div class="mt-5 border-l-4 border-[#b4232b] bg-white p-4" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
          <h4 id="fixture-result-title" class="text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Choose a fixture above</h4>
          <p id="fixture-result-detail" class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700">The highlighted route will show how that fixture generally connects to the home's larger drain system.</p>
          <p id="fixture-result-clue" class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold leading-6 text-slate-800"></p>
          <p id="fixture-result-next" class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-700"></p>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">This guide cannot see inside your pipes or confirm the blockage location. If sewage is coming up through a basement floor drain, stop using water and call A-1 Drain Cleaning at <a class="font-bold underline" href="tel:+16415302728">641-530-2728</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
  <style>
    .route-highlight path { fill:none; stroke:#d97706; stroke-width:9; stroke-linecap:round; stroke-linejoin:round; opacity:0; transition:opacity .18s ease; }
    .route-highlight.is-active path { opacity:1; }
    .fixture-choice[aria-pressed="true"] { border-color:#1A1A68; background:#1A1A68; color:#fff; }
    @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.route-highlight path{transition:none}}
  </style>
  <script>
    const choices = document.querySelectorAll('.fixture-choice');
    const routes = document.querySelectorAll('.route-highlight');
    const title = document.getElementById('fixture-result-title');
    const detail = document.getElementById('fixture-result-detail');
    const clue = document.getElementById('fixture-result-clue');
    const next = document.getElementById('fixture-result-next');

    choices.forEach((choice) => {
      choice.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const route = choice.dataset.route;
        choices.forEach((item) => item.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(item === choice)));
        routes.forEach((item) => item.classList.toggle('is-active', item.dataset.route === route));
        title.textContent = choice.dataset.title || '';
        detail.textContent = choice.dataset.detail || '';
        clue.textContent = choice.dataset.clue || '';
        next.textContent = choice.dataset.next || '';
      });
    });
  </script>
</section>
